# SSH keys allowed to sign release tags (#62, decision D-2).
#
# `Release: Verify` (.github/workflows/release.yml) refuses a v* tag, release
# candidates included, unless it is an annotated tag signed with a key listed
# here. It runs, from the tagged commit:
#
#   git -c gpg.format=ssh -c gpg.ssh.allowedSignersFile=.github/allowed_signers verify-tag <tag>
#
# Pull requests and dry runs check that this file parses
# (scripts/verify-tag-signature.sh).
#
# Format: the ALLOWED SIGNERS section of ssh-keygen(1). One key per line:
#
#   principal namespaces="git" key-type base64-key [comment]
#
# for example (the key shortened):
#
#   auzroz namespaces="git" ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3Nza...
#
# - principal: a label for the signer, such as their GitHub login. It is used
#   in messages only and doesn't have to match the tagger's email. This file is
#   public: put no email address here;
# - namespaces="git": the key may sign git objects only;
# - key-type and base64-key: the first two fields of the public key file, for
#   example from `cut -d' ' -f1-2 ~/.ssh/id_ed25519_signing.pub`.
#
# Lines starting with # and blank lines are ignored. A key is added or removed
# by a pull request; the file on the tagged commit is the one that counts.
#
# No key is listed yet, so every tag fails until the maintainer adds theirs.
